Title: Fix wrong erg validate example in README quick-start
Created: 2026-05-29
Author: Claude

--- log ---
2026-05-29T15:10Z Claude created — UX audit finding F01 (verified); first binary example is broken

--- body ---
## Context

The UX audit (0152, PR #174) found that the README's "Quick start (with
the erg binary)" section gives a broken first example. README line ~119
shows:

```
tickets/erg validate 01
```

`erg validate` takes file *paths*, not IDs. Running it produces:

```
WARNING: skipping 01 (stat 01: no such file or directory)
No .erg files found.
```

and exits 0 — so it *looks* like validation passed when nothing was
validated. This is the first command a user runs after installing the
binary, and it silently does nothing. Found independently by the beginner
and expert personas; reproduced.

## Relevant files

- `README.md` — the "Quick start (with the erg binary)" section (~line 117)
- `tests/test_docs.sh` — doc-consistency tests (candidate guard location)

## Actions

1. Change the README example to a working invocation that validates the
   ticket created by the zero-install demo, e.g.:
   `tickets/erg validate tickets/0001-add-auth.erg`
   (or `tickets/erg check tickets/` for directory-level validation —
   pick whichever the surrounding prose intends).
2. Scan the README for any other `validate <ID>` style examples and fix
   them in the same commit (rename/refactor sweep over the doc section).

## Test

Add a guard (in `tests/test_docs.sh` or `test_ux.sh`) that extracts the
`erg validate` example from README and asserts it does not pass a bare
2-digit ID. Source-inspection form (no subprocess):

```sh
if grep -Eq 'erg validate [0-9]{1,3}( |$)' README.md; then
    fail "README has an erg validate example with a bare ID (takes paths)"
else
    pass "README erg validate examples use file paths"
fi
```

Catches the wrong implementation (bare-ID example), not merely a
different wording.

## Verification

- [ ] README quick-start `validate` example uses a real file path
- [ ] The corrected command actually validates the demo ticket (exit 0,
      reports a file checked)
- [ ] No remaining `validate <ID>` examples in README
- [ ] Guard test fails against the pre-fix README, passes after

## Invariants

- Keep the quick-start consistent with the zero-install demo above it
  (the file it validates must be the one the demo creates).
- `make test` / `make validate` stay green.

## Exit criteria

- The README's first binary example is a working command, and a test
  guards against bare-ID `validate` examples returning.
